        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamplifier",
        "description": "NE5532 dual low-noise op-amp used as the low-level preamplifier stage for the compact audio amplifier. This module accepts the external audio input, performs the main voltage amplification needed to reach the overall target gain range together with the following power stage, and drives the LM386 input through an inter-stage audio path. The first amplifier channel should be treated as the primary preamp signal path; the second channel may be left unused or later assigned to buffering, filtering, or bias support only if downstream design confirms a valid passive network. Because the brief specifies a single 9V supply while NE5532 has only VCC_P and VCC_N pins in the provided data, this module must operate from VIN_9V and GND-referenced single-supply biasing implemented by downstream passive support; no negative rail generator exists in the component list. Input and output signal paths are analog and must preserve low-noise routing intent relative to the higher-current speaker drive stage.",
        "id": "preamplifier"
      },
