        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_amplifier",
        "description": "LM386 low-voltage audio power amplifier used as the final stage to drive the 8-ohm speaker from the single VIN_9V supply. This module receives the preamplified analog signal from the NE5532 stage at its signal input, applies its own gain-setting network through the provided GAIN_1 and GAIN_2 pins as needed to reach the overall target gain of about 100x-200x, and produces a speaker-drive output from VOUT. The IN_NEG, BYPASS, and gain-control related behavior depend on downstream passive implementation and must be planned to support stable single-supply audio operation. This module is the high-current audio output domain, so its output return currents should be kept separated in routing intent from the low-level preamplifier input path except for the shared GND system reference. The speaker load is external to the provided component list, so the output remains exposed as a module interface.",
